// PARAM: --analysis int --int-refinement never
// Int answers a check component by component, as Goblint's IntDomTuple
// does, so the mode reaches a check through what the stored states know. A
// join shows the difference.
//
// On the true arm of y + 1 == 3, the inverses of == and + teach Parity and
// Congruence that y = 2, and Interval and Sign learn nothing. A refinement
// round hands the singleton to Interval, so the join with y = 4 keeps [2,4]
// and proves y > 0. Without refinement the join keeps only y = 0 (mod 2).
//
// once and fixpoint agree here, and on every program we tried: each later
// operation refines again, which closes the gap one round leaves. That gap is
// visible on single values (Int_Refinement_Control.thy,
// refinement_once_not_fixpoint).
// Under never, the check is not proved.
fun main() {
  y = __voblint_nondet_int();
  if (y + 1 == 3) {
    x = 0;
  } else {
    y = 4;
  }
  __voblint_check(y > 0); // UNKNOWN
}
